---
import { execution, lanes, toolNames } from '../labs/gateway/model';
import '../labs/gateway/gateway.css';
import GatewayIcon from '../labs/gateway/GatewayIcon.astro';
---
<section class="gl" data-gateway-lab aria-labelledby="gl-title" data-outcome="ready">
  <div class="gl-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Recorded execution / interactive replay</p><h2 id="gl-title">The right tools<br /><em>for this task.</em></h2></div><p>Choose a fictional task. Try an action. Inspect the actual gateway’s response from the local test.</p></div>
  <div class="gl-lanes" role="group" aria-label="Choose a fictional task">{Object.entries(lanes).map(([key, lane], i) => <button type="button" class="gl-lane" data-lane={key} aria-pressed={key === 'scout'}><span class="gl-lane-number">0{i + 1}</span><span><strong>{lane.title}</strong><span>{lane.copy}</span><small>Fictional user {lane.user} · {key === 'scout' ? 'Scout' : 'Host'}</small></span><span class="gl-lane-check"><GatewayIcon name="external" /></span></button>)}</div>
  <div class="gl-workspace">
    <article class="gl-toolbox"><header><p class="eyebrow">Published tools</p><span data-catalog-count>1 tool</span></header><ul data-tools>{toolNames('scout-catalog').map(name => <li><GatewayIcon name="music" /><code>{name}</code></li>)}</ul><p class="gl-catalog-note">A smaller catalog gives the model a focused starting point. Calls are checked again.</p><div class="gl-actions" data-actions>{lanes.scout.actions.map(action => <button type="button" data-attempt={action.key}>{action.label}<GatewayIcon /></button>)}</div></article>
    <article class="gl-boundary" aria-labelledby="gl-boundary-title"><header><p class="eyebrow" id="gl-boundary-title">The gateway boundary</p><span data-result-badge>Ready to replay</span></header><div class="gl-path" aria-hidden="true"><div class="gl-endpoint"><span class="gl-orb">01</span><strong>Task</strong><small data-path-user>user 101</small></div><span class="gl-wire gl-wire-in"><i></i></span><div class="gl-gate"><span class="gl-gate-symbol"><GatewayIcon name="shield" /></span><strong>Gateway</strong><small data-gate-result>checks the request</small></div><span class="gl-wire gl-wire-out"><i></i></span><div class="gl-endpoint gl-backend"><span class="gl-orb">02</span><strong>Local backend</strong><small data-path-backend>fictional music</small></div></div><div class="gl-result" aria-live="polite"><h3 data-result-title>What should this task be able to do?</h3><p data-result-copy>Find tracks, then try to add one. The second action is outside the Scout’s published tool set.</p></div><div class="gl-proof"><div><span>Observed response</span><strong data-http>—</strong></div><div><span>Upstream tool calls</span><strong data-forwarded>—</strong></div><div><span>Backend user</span><strong data-backend-user>—</strong></div></div></article>
  </div>
  <div class="gl-identity"><GatewayIcon name="arrow" /><div><strong>The request also claims to be someone else.</strong><p>The recorded request supplies <code>_meta.user_id: <span data-claimed-user>202</span></code>. The authenticated caller is user <span data-auth-user>101</span>. On an allowed call, the gateway replaces that claim before forwarding.</p></div></div>
  <p class="gl-disclosure">These controls replay recorded results. The full archived gateway ran locally; auth answers, user records, permission settings and music operations were fictional fixtures. Nothing plays, changes volume or calls a live service here.</p>
  <p data-fallback class="gl-disclosure">With JavaScript off, use the captured request transcript and receipt below.</p>
  <details class="gl-inspect" data-inspect><summary><GatewayIcon name="expand" />Inspect this recorded request <span data-inspect-label>Choose an action first</span></summary><div class="gl-inspect-meta"><code data-record-path>/soundtrack-scout/mcp</code><span data-observed-duration>Observed duration appears after a replay</span></div><div class="gl-payloads"><div><h3>Sent to the gateway</h3><pre data-request>Choose an action to see its actual request.</pre></div><div><h3>Returned to the caller</h3><pre data-response>Choose an action to see its actual response.</pre></div></div><p data-counter-proof>The local backend counted every tool call.</p><a href="/media/gateway/transcript.txt">Complete captured transcript <GatewayIcon name="external" /></a></details>
  <details class="gl-native"><summary><GatewayIcon name="expand" />A native profile has a different boundary <span>Explore the actual fallback behavior</span></summary><div class="gl-native-intro"><h3>Profiles curate the catalog.<br />User policy still decides access.</h3><p>The same <code>/mcp/task</code> URL resolved to different native tools for two fictional users. The actual MCP server registered only those tools. A guessed off-profile tool did not run its handler.</p><p>Unknown profile names fall back to the master catalog. A failed fresh profile lookup does too. A failed fresh permission lookup blocks tool execution. That distinction matters.</p></div><div class="gl-native-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Replay native profile checks"><button data-native="native-scout-profile">Scout profile</button><button data-native="native-host-profile">Host profile</button><button data-native="native-scout-off-profile">Off-profile call</button><button data-native="native-unknown-profile-fallback">Unknown profile</button><button data-native="native-outage-catalog-fallback">Catalog during outage</button><button data-native="native-outage-call-fails-closed">Call during outage</button></div><div class="gl-native-result" aria-live="polite"><p data-native-title>Select a recorded native request.</p><p data-native-copy>Explore its catalog or execution result.</p><pre data-native-response hidden></pre></div></details>
  <details class="gl-receipt"><summary><GatewayIcon name="expand" />What ran, what was substituted <span>17 asserted requests · actual source</span></summary><div class="gl-receipt-grid"><div><h3>The actual gateway</h3><ul>{execution.fixture.real.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><dl><dt>Source</dt><dd><code>{execution.source.commit}</code></dd><dt>Source tag</dt><dd>{execution.source.tag}</dd><dt>Observed run</dt><dd>{execution.executed_at.replace('T', ' ').slice(0,19)} UTC</dd><dt>Verification</dt><dd>17 asserted HTTP/MCP requests. 65 existing tests passed across 6 suites. Gateway exited 0.</dd></dl></div><div><h3>The local substitutes</h3><ul>{execution.fixture.replaced.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><h3>Scope of this proof</h3><p>No real credentials, private catalog, external provider, production Redis or notification delivery. The fixture used an explicit loopback request allowlist. Caller bearer tokens were absent at the fake music backend.</p><p>OAuth consent and issuance, real provider credential lookup, batch identity isolation, native engine permissions and cache refresh timing were outside this run.</p><p>The public receipt keeps tool-call response bodies and counters. Catalogs are shortened to actual tool names, with hashes of the raw recorded catalog responses.</p><a class="text-link" href="/media/gateway/receipt.json" download>Recorded receipt <GatewayIcon name="download" /></a></div></div></details>
</section>
<script>import { initGateway } from '../labs/gateway/controller'; document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-gateway-lab]').forEach(initGateway);</script>
